{"assignees":[],"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Problem\n\nIn the Pull Requests column a PR's state icon only distinguishes open (`●` green), merged (`⊕`) and closed (`✓` red). Whether an open PR is still a **draft**, and whether it has been **approved** / had **changes requested**, is shown as trailing badges (`✓` / `✗` / `[draft]`) after the title and the assignee / reviewer names. In a narrow column those badges are the first thing to be cut off, so a draft PR and a reviewed PR look the same as any other open PR.\n\n## Proposal\n\nMake both facts visible at the *front* of the row, where they survive any width:\n\n- **Draft** — a draft PR gets its own state icon and color instead of the green `●`: `◌` in dark gray (the same hollow / dimmed treatment GitHub uses). The trailing `[draft]` badge is removed. Merged / closed stay as they are.\n- **Review decision** — a fixed one-column mark right after the state icon: `✓` green for `APPROVED`, `✗` red for `CHANGES_REQUESTED`, `◯` yellow for `REVIEW_REQUIRED`, blank otherwise (no decision / branch protection off). The trailing `✓` / `✗` badges are removed.\n\n```text\n ● ✓ #210 GitHub view: show assignees and reviewers @td72\n ◌   #212 WIP: highlight my items @td72 → carol\n ● ✗ #198 Release 0.17.0\n```\n\n- The PR detail header gets a `DRAFT` badge next to the existing `✓ APPROVED` / `✗ CHANGES REQUESTED` / `◯ REVIEW REQUIRED` badges.\n- Docs (README en/ja, guide `views-github.md` en/ja) describe the icons; the PR tape is re-recorded so the GIF shows a draft PR if the fixtures contain one.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Pure rendering change: `isDraft` and `reviewDecision` are already fetched by `gh pr list` / `gh pr view`.\n- Should land before #209 so the \"mine\" highlight is built on the final row layout.\n","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-11-04T10:43:29Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":212,"state":"CLOSED","title":"GitHub view: show a PR's draft state and review decision at a glance"}
